Appendix C — Small‑Gain ISS Proof for the Nonlinear Delayed GRU

C.1 Error Dynamics

Let \mathbf{h}^\star be the ideal fixed point, and \mathbf{e}^{(t)} = \mathbf{h}^{(t)} - \mathbf{h}^\star. The GRU update is

\mathbf{e}^{(t)} = W_{\text{rec}}\phi(\mathbf{e}^{(t-1)}) + \sum_j A_{ij}\psi(\mathbf{e}^{(t-\tau_{ji})}) + \nu^{(t)},

where \phi,\psi are Lipschitz with constants L_\phi,L_\psi\le 1.

C.2 Small‑Gain Theorem for Delayed Networks

We apply the trajectory‑based small‑gain theorem for delayed neural fields (Chairez, 2016). Define the ISS‑Lyapunov function V(\mathbf{e}) = \|\mathbf{e}\|. Then

\|\mathbf{e}^{(t)}\| \le \gamma_{\text{rec}}\|\mathbf{e}^{(t-1)}\| + \gamma_{\text{delay}}\max_{k}\|\mathbf{e}^{(t-\tau_k)}\| + \|\nu^{(t)}\|.

Iterating and using \gamma_{\text{rec}}+\gamma_{\text{delay}}\tau_{\max}<1, we obtain the exponential ISS bound

\|\mathbf{e}^{(t)}\| \le M\lambda^t\|\mathbf{e}^{(0)}\| + \frac{\gamma_{\text{ISS}}}{1-\lambda}\|\nu\|_\infty,

with \gamma_{\text{ISS}} = \gamma_{\text{delay}}/(1-\gamma_{\text{rec}}) and \lambda = \gamma_{\text{rec}}+\gamma_{\text{delay}}\tau_{\max}.

