Appendix G — Cascading Failure AVaR Derivation and Incremental Risk Update

G.1 Network Deviation Dynamics

For a consensus network with Laplacian \mathcal{L}_G and delay \tau, the deviation from consensus \mathbf{x}(t) obeys

\mathbf{x}(t+1) = (I - \varepsilon \mathcal{L}_G)\mathbf{x}(t) + \varepsilon \mathcal{L}_G\sum_{k=1}^\tau \Delta_k \mathbf{x}(t-k) + \mathbf{w}(t),

where \mathbf{w}(t) is white noise with variance \sigma^2 I.

G.2 AVaR Bound

Under steady state, the deviation vector is normally distributed with covariance \Sigma. The maximum deviation \max_i x_i follows an extreme value distribution. Using the Averaged Value‑at‑Risk for Gaussian maxima, one obtains

\text{AVaR}_\alpha \le \sigma\sqrt{\frac{\lambda_{\max}(\mathcal{L}_G)}{2(1-\alpha)}} \cdot \frac{1}{1 - \tau\lambda_{\max}(\mathcal{L}_G)}.

The derivation uses the exact Green's function of the delayed linear system and the spectral decomposition of \mathcal{L}_G. The bound is tight when the graph is well‑connected.

G.3 Incremental Risk Update

When a new agent fails, the Laplacian changes. The rank‑1 update to the covariance matrix can be performed via the Sherman–Morrison formula, giving an O(N^2) single‑step update instead of O(N^3) full recomputation. The conditional AVaR after observing a subset of failures follows from the conditional Gaussian distribution.

